WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.020
I'm going!

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.470
Come back safely!

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.270
<i>It's been two years since 
Itsuka came to Ryokushou.</i>

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:18.700
<i>Lately, it doesn't seem like she's been 
going to the station to look for her father.</i>

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.500
<i>I wonder if it's because she's 
started looking toward the future...</i>

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.520
Itsuka-chan! Morning!

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.140
<i>or if it's because she's given up.</i>

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.100
Morning!

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.250
Morning!

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.250
<b>For Pedestrians and Cyclists</b>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.960
It's warm today, isn't it?

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.220
Well, it is March already.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.220
Oh, yeah. Itsuka-chan, your 
birthday's this month, right?

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.810
Y-Yeah.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:41.180
Here.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:46.190
<b>Exclusively for Nagomu-san
3/26
Going Somewhere Together
 Ticket</b>

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.530
March twenty-sixth?

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.820
Let me just say that if you lose it,
 it becomes invalid, okay?

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:55.160
Okay. It's a promise.

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:01.550
If you're lying, I'll make 
you swallow a thousand yokan.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:03.820
That'd be rough.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:17.840
<b>Recipe for
 Happiness</b>

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:44.010
<b>Red Sea Bream for a Spring Dawn</b>

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:48.020
Narrow Window

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:48.020
Early Wins

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:48.020
Take Friends

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:48.020
Itsuka's Birthday

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.020
At the end of this month, 
on the twenty-sixth...

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:50.360
That's Itsuka-chan's birthday, right?

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.260
We'll have to make lots of 
chicken karaage this year, too.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.300
What will we do about the cake?

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.980
Yes... I wonder if the same as 
last year will be all right.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.970
What do children these days like?

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:04.760
Um...

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.040
About the cake...

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.310
What about making it out of wagashi?

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:10.660
That sounds good!

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.590
When I worked at Hachiten, 
we got some orders for those.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.670
Then, shall we brainstorm together?

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.660
Y-Yes, sir!

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.890
What are you doing?

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.680
It's almost here.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.430
<b>Exclusively for Nagomu-san
3/26
Going Somewhere Together
 Ticket</b>

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:30.430
At last, the time for 
me to use this has come!

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:31.470
What is that?

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:36.840
I've been thinking and thinking 
about where I'll take her!

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.440
Apparently, Itsuka gave it 
to him for his birthday.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.440
He said it's a "Going 
Somewhere Together Ticket."

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.850
Every morning I look at this 
and think, "Is this a dream?"

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:42.910
Nagomu-san...

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.650
Is it all right if I find this off-putting?

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.920
What's going on? Everyone's all together.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.790
If you're happy, that's the
 most important thing.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:55.540
Dad, what're you doing?

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:59.480
There's a hanami festival coming 
up at the Nonoguchi Jinja, right?

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.260
I'm checking the sweets that 
are meant for the tea party.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.220
Really? Oh, there's sakura 
mochi in the order, too.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:09.360
Speaking of which, how was 
it while you were in Tokyo?

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:10.720
Was it all Choumeiji-style?

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:13.980
Um... Well, there were 
Choumeiji-style ones, too.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:18.120
In the Kanto area, they're made of an 
wrapped in a thin skin cooked in a pan.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:20.730
A temple called Choumeiji used 
to sell them at their gate.

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:22.280
I think that's where the name came from.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:26.040
In the Kansai area, an is wrapped 
in steamed doumyoji rice flour,

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.870
named in honor of Doumyouji Temple.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.360
We don't see the Choumeiji-style 
much around here,

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:33.000
but lots of places in Tokyo sold both kinds.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.110
Really...

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:37.630
But you seem to be staying nicely 
within your comfort zone.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:44.300
<b>Spring's Arrival</b>

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.770
Like this Spring's Arrival, for example.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:41.580
If you added gold leaf to make it look like

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.300
sunlight was striking it, 
that would be nice, right?

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.680
<i>Gold leaf...</i>

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.680
Don't just say things 
as they come to you!

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:54.380
If you carelessly use gold leaf and ruin the 
balance of the piece, it'll only look crass!

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:55.850
Yes, sir...

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:59.050
Try saying that after you've gained 
some knowledge and experience!

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:00.950
Yes, I will.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:09.850
Gramps, wouldn't it be better to 
make the color of this darker?

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:12.250
It's making the white of 
the jouyo manju seem dingy.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:16.940
He's always been so impudent...

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:22.050
<b>Nightingale</b>

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:22.050
<b>Budding Crimson</b>

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:22.050
<b>Flowing</b>

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:20.240
Welcome!

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:22.050
Have you finished the 
next round of prep work?

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.320
The manju are done steaming!

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.720
Masa-san, take care of the next batch for me!

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.680
Yes, sir!

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.430
I've made some extra boxes!

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.870
What about the inventory check?

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.060
Finished!

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.300
Good. Now, drain off the bitterness.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.160
Yes, sir.

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:58.580
Itsuka, what are you doing?

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:02.910
Um, I was going to take a bath, and I saw
 that the workshop lights were on.

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:06.150
Oh, Nagomu is cooking an.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.200
Cooking an?

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:11.610
I thought it would be a while off yet,

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:14.430
but Otousan just isn't good 
at restraining himself.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:15.350
What?

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:19.500
He came home saying stupid stuff about 
how he'd inherit the shop from me.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.230
I'll run him ragged doing 
chores for a full three years!

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:25.230
He said all of that, and yet...

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:28.350
Starting a few days ago, I saw 
him staring at the calendar.

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.030
I wondered what he was doing.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:33.800
But today happens to be a Day of 
Future Harvests, so we can expect good luck.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.490
Day of Future Harvests?

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:39.550
A single grain of unhulled rice can 
grow into many times that amount.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:42.590
So this is a day that can bring 
great returns in the future.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:45.180
The exact dates change every year, though.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:48.400
Starting a new job, 
opening a store, planting seeds,

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.640
spending or investing money... It's a day 
they say is good for that sort of thing.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.420
<i>So his face can look like that, too.</i>

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:02.270
<i>When he first came back, 
he was unreliable, but...</i>

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:06.230
<i>I guess it has been a year since then.</i>

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.040
Come now. Go take your bath.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:11.880
Yes, I will.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:17.450
You're asking what Itsuka-chan 
and I talk about?

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:19.600
Normal stuff.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:21.630
And what is that "normal stuff"?

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:25.760
What do the dads in this world talk about 
with their daughters? Dreams? Wishes?

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:28.960
Wouldn't it be things 
like school and friends?

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:32.220
What are you guys talking about in secret?

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:36.330
Just work assignments and going out 
drinking together again! Stuff like that!

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:37.180
That's right! That's right!

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:40.760
If you slack off too much, the master's 
fists are going to come flying.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.300
Yes, you're right.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.880
Oh, Itsuka!

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:46.030
About tomorrow...

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:47.340
Tomorrow?

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:49.560
Um, well...

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:52.140
Don't oversleep.

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:55.240
<i>It wasn't a dream!</i>

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.490
<i>He's so easy to read!</i>

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:03.250
<i>We have to travel as efficiently 
as possible, right?</i>

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:32.820
<b>Today,
\hfor personal
\h\hreasons,
\h\h\hwe will
\h\h\h\hbe closed.

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:35.470
Good morning.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:36.780
Morning.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.260
Happy birthday.

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:41.200
Thank you!

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:43.850
A present arrived from your mother.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:47.780
It says it's from London. 
I wonder what it could be.

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:51.920
Oh my!

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:55.480
How lovely. It suits you very well.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:57.900
Where's Nagomu-san?

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:01.290
Nagomu? He's probably 
still sleeping, isn't he?

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:07.900
<i>Lately he's been working until 
late at night. Maybe he's tired.</i>

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:12.190
Hey. Happy birthday, Itsuka.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:14.320
Thank you.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.400
So you were awake. How will you be going?

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:20.560
We'll drive. I just went and got gas.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.820
Once Itsuka's finished breakfast, 
we can take our time and head out.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:26.720
Be careful, though it seems 
like the weather will be nice.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:27.870
Yes, we will.

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:29.620
Itsuka...

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:33.280
A little spending money. Take it with you.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:35.590
It's okay. I'll pay for everything.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:38.280
If you get fed up, use that
 and come back home.

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:39.850
You're saying that so I can hear it?

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:45.210
Come home quickly. We'll get the 
cake and chicken karaage ready.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:46.600
All right.

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:50.110
Where are we going?

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.340
Somewhere I invited you to before.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:06.940
Do you mean Hirakata Park?

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:10.130
That's right. Back then you 
were against the idea, but...

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:12.380
How about Hirakata Park?

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:15.030
They've got a ride called 
Pachanga that's really popular!

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:19.340
To think the day would come that 
we'd be going together like this...

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:21.090
Please keep looking ahead of us! Look!

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:24.430
Yes. That's good.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.430
Thank you!

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:33.150
For Itsuka's birthday present, 
I made her a cell phone strap.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.150
Oh my. How nice!

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:38.680
This is from all the employees. 
It's a children's makeup set.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:41.960
Makeup? Saki-kun, you seem 
quite knowledgeable about that.

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:43.450
Huh? Oh, um, well...

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.620
Nagomu-san and Itsuka-chan should 
be getting there soon, right?

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:48.870
Yes, I think so.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:59.030
Itsuka!

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:01.430
What's wrong?

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:05.500
I-It's nothing!

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:11.790
I'm so glad we made it 
here without any problems!

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:13.230
Made it here?

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:17.530
I mean! You know! It's the first 
time I've driven you anywhere,

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:19.780
and I was not freaked out at all!

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:23.030
So that's why you replied in broken 
sentences when I spoke to you.

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:25.450
Well, I'm glad we arrived safely.

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:30.080
<i>Uh-oh. When she's like this, 
things fall apart fast.</i>

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:33.950
So, if we're going to 
talk about school first,

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:34.110
<i>I did run a simulation in 
my head before I slept.</i>

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:36.410
then I'll ask what's 
popular these days and...

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:36.410
<i>But I fell asleep right away.</i>

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:42.470
<i>No! I still have my book of secrets.</i>

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:50.020
Itsuka.

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:51.770
What should we ride first?

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:54.550
Hmm, let's see...

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:00.780
Is someone there?

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:02.110
No!

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:05.530
Oh, Nagomu-san, have you been here before?

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:11.480
Back in high school. I came 
with friends and our senpais.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.750
How about you, Itsuka? 
Have you been here before?

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:16.330
No, I haven't.

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:20.650
Really? Then I'm glad I brought you.

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:23.060
Then, what should we ride first?

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.340
Well, let's see...

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:26.840
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:30.100
<i>I asked Saki-kun to pick out 
the ones Itsuka might like!</i>

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.270
<b>Hmmmm</b>

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.270
<b>Hmmmm</b>

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.270
<b>Hmmmm</b>

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.270
<b>Hmmmm</b>

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.270
<b>Hmmmm</b>

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.270
<b>Hmmmm</b>

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:31.640
<i>If Itsuka says...</i>

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:32.880
I want to ride Pachanga!

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:33.810
<i>Then...</i>

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:37.350
<i>I've drawn everything out on the map so that 
we can get there as quickly as possible!</i>

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:41.750
Huh?

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:43.720
What?

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:48.480
<i>What? When was the last time I checked it?</i>

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:50.040
<i>This morning? Where?</i>

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:52.950
<i>In bed.</i>

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:55.080
<i>And I folded them up together...</i>

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:58.210
<b>Gloom</b>

00:12:56.870 --> 00:12:58.210
<i>He's so easy to read.</i>

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:00.470
Nagomu-san...

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:04.490
You're trying way too hard 
to be considerate. It's weird.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:06.000
It's making me uncomfortable.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.970
But today is all about you, Itsuka.

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:10.270
I <i>will</i> go home, you know.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:11.430
Right. Understood.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:14.430
Nagomu-san, you can just 
be the way you always are.

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:16.070
Let's go.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.540
Yes, ma'am.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:41.170
Okay! Where should we go next?

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:43.760
Nagomu-san, how about your stomach?

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:44.440
Huh?

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:48.950
My stomach noticed when 
you asked... What should we eat?

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.930
Where should we go?

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:54.490
<i>Now that I've told him he can 
just be the way he always is,</i>

00:13:54.490 --> 00:13:57.060
<i>I can't also tell him to calm down a little.</i>

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:02.700
The look on your face is a little stiff.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:06.070
What was that, after secretly 
taking someone's picture?

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:08.360
Hey! People might misunderstand!

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:12.950
It's for your mother. She asked
 me to show her pictures.

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:18.120
I wish you were kinda playing around more.

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:21.630
<i>When I'm with someone who plays around 
as much as you, that's impossible!</i>

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:22.670
Excuse me!

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:23.710
Yes?

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:25.840
Would you take a picture for me?

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:26.670
What?

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:30.620
To commemorate this! Now, come on! Pose!

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:33.600
If the father could please move a 
little more toward the center...

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:34.720
"Father"!

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.020
He isn't my father!

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:39.880
I-I'm so sorry! He's so young that 
I did think I might be mistaken.

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:42.270
Father, huh?

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:43.610
Please don't be so happy about it.

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:46.190
Do we really look like that?

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:47.800
Please deny it!

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:50.220
Um, is it all right to take the picture?

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.740
It's just about time.

00:15:30.560 --> 00:15:32.440
Are you sure you don't 
want to buy souvenirs?

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:33.260
Yes.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:34.580
In that case...

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:38.870
I'll call and tell them we're 
coming back. Just a minute, okay?

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:42.260
Oh, Mom? Yeah, it's me.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:44.380
Mama?

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:56.460
There you are!

00:15:56.460 --> 00:15:58.250
Mama! Mama!

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:00.300
I'm so sorry I let go of your hand!

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:02.900
I was talking, so I wasn't paying attention!

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:07.560
I'm so glad! Is she all right?

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.480
Nagomu-san?

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:24.620
Where are you?

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:26.020
Nagomu-san?

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:29.020
<i>Did he head toward the parking lot?</i>

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:32.590
<i>No. It's probably better if 
I don't move around too much.</i>

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:37.460
<i>After a little while, I'll go
 to the information center.</i>

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:42.010
<i>And if I need it, I have the 
spending money the old man gave me.</i>

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:46.340
<i>Even alone, I'll be able 
to do something about this.</i>

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:07.420
Yeah. Got i—

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:11.670
Itsuka?

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:17.590
Oh, Mom, sorry. Yeah. We should
 be back around then.

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:23.310
<i>He was so close. I was 
the one who looked away.</i>

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:19.260
Okay, bye.

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:24.870
What's wrong?

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:28.150
Nothing's wrong.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:32.780
Well, not that I mind.

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:37.480
Just don't stretch my clothes out, okay?

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:49.080
Man, that was fun. Wasn't it, Itsuka?

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.070
Yes.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:54.590
<b>Taiyaki</b>

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:54.590
Taiyaki

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:54.590
<b>Taiyaki</b>

00:17:51.490 --> 00:17:53.750
There's a taiyaki vendor.

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:59.090
When I came here before, Papa bought me some.

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:02.100
I don't know if it's the 
same stall or not, though.

00:18:02.380 --> 00:18:04.280
Wow, really?

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:06.090
Huh? I, um...

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:08.910
I mean, yes, I came before, 
but I was little, so I forgot—

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.690
Should we buy some? I mean, 
since we're here and everything.

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:11.550
Welcome!

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:14.190
Excuse me. Can I have two with anko?

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.780
Thank you! That'll be 240 yen.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:19.820
Here you go.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.180
Thanks.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:23.280
Here, Itsuka.

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:27.020
How nice! You came to play 
here with your father, huh?

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:30.240
<i>Oh, she's gonna deny it again, right?</i>

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:31.420
Thank you.

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:32.290
Huh?

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:37.830
Itsuka, are you all right with...?

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:40.090
Every single time is too much trouble.

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:43.300
For today, it's fine.

00:18:45.510 --> 00:18:46.730
I see.

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:51.930
Well, let's hurry home. Everyone's waiting.

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:52.870
Yes.

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:55.610
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:55.610
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.310
It's from Nagomu.

00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:02.500
What did he say?

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:06.060
It seems they enjoyed their outing.

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:08.140
I'm so glad.

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:09.770
That's a relief.

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:13.560
Well, then, I suppose I should start 
frying up the chicken karaage.

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:15.310
I'll help!

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:16.880
S-So will I!

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.330
I'm back!

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:36.120
They're back.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.500
What a feast!

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:42.570
Wow!

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:44.420
There's a cake, too.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:45.830
<b>Itsuka
 Happy Birthday</b>

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:48.200
That's amazing! A wagashi cake!

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.700
Thank you so much!

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:53.460
Well, now, everyone must be hungry.

00:19:53.890 --> 00:19:55.160
Let's get started.

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:59.590
Happy birthday!

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:02.330
Th-Thank you.

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:05.620
You've got a heap of presents there!

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.500
Here. This is from me.

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:10.600
You can open it now.

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:14.030
Oh! How cute!

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:15.100
It really is!

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:18.560
Thank you, Nagomu-san.

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:21.740
What's this? I thought 
I was your father today!

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:22.910
Father?

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:23.500
What?

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:27.740
The thing is, people mistook me for 
her dad, and Itsuka said it was okay!

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:29.370
Just for today, understand?

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.980
But there's only a little bit of today left!

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:34.030
Give me an extension!

00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:35.210
No!

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:37.460
Come, Itsuka.

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:40.500
Forget about Nagomu. Eat whatever you like.

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:43.040
And you, Nagomu? What will you drink?

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:47.470
<b>Itsuka
 Happy Birthday</b>

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:44.800
Oh, I guess I'll have a beer.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:45.900
Make it a low-malt happoushu instead.

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:47.470
Aw, c'mon!

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:48.550
What are you doing?

00:22:49.250 --> 00:22:51.710
Nothing in particular.

00:22:51.710 --> 00:22:54.860
I sent pictures from today to your mother.

00:22:54.860 --> 00:22:56.810
Oh, thanks.

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:03.050
And about your father...

00:23:03.050 --> 00:23:07.470
It's only that now isn't the time. 
I'm sure that one day you'll see him again.

00:23:07.470 --> 00:23:08.590
How did you...

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:11.520
Of course I know.

00:23:11.520 --> 00:23:15.300
You were looking for your father
 at Hirakata Park, too, right?

00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:19.540
And... the first time I met you, too, I guess.

00:23:20.310 --> 00:23:21.770
Still...

00:23:21.770 --> 00:23:25.220
For now, if you can relax and feel 
safe here, that's enough, right?

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:28.630
Nagomu-san, you still don't understand me.

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:34.140
It's because I feel safe 
that I can wait here.

00:23:37.700 --> 00:23:39.210
Well, that's true.

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:43.750
I still have a lot of training to do.

00:23:46.360 --> 00:23:49.280
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:23:46.360 --> 00:23:49.280
<b>Ryokushou</b>
